<title>ITALY: Italy's Milan sees Dec CPI at 2.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Milan sees Dec CPI at 2.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Milan said its December consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Milan's inflation rate was 0.3 percent and 2.7 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Milan is one of 10 Italian cities to publish inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 19.1 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.3)     2.7  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0  (-0.3)     3.0  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4   (0.3)     3.7  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.1   (0.7)     9.1  (9.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.9)     2.4  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     2.2  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.1   (0.4)    -0.9 (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.6  (-0.2)     1.7  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (2.2)     2.6  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1   (0.2)     3.7  (3.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.1)     1.8  (1.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
